    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-magenta);\" data-correct=\"C\" data-multi=\"\" data-rationale=\"Lambda functions can be invoked from S3 events and can read from S3 buckets. An event-based invocation would allow for the S3 objects to be processed as soon as they arrive. For more information about invoking a Lambda function from S3, see Tutorial: Using an Amazon S3 trigger to invoke a Lambda function.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;A company has an inventory system that receives sporadic inventory updates from a fulfillment system in the form of large JSON files. While many files can be sent in a short time period, days can pass when no files are sent. The company wants to process these files as soon as they arrive. Which solution will meet these requirements?&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;Lambda functions can connect to Amazon EFS file systems. However, Amazon EFS file system changes cannot invoke Lambda functions. For more information about using Lambda functions with Amazon EFS, see Using Amazon EFS with Lambda.&quot;, &quot;Lambda functions can run on a schedule and connect to Amazon EFS file systems. However, a scheduled/polling process would not process the files as soon as they arrive. For more information about using Lambda functions with Amazon EFS, see Using Amazon EFS with Lambda.&quot;, &quot;Lambda functions can be invoked from S3 events and can read from S3 buckets. An event-based invocation would allow for the S3 objects to be processed as soon as they arrive. For more information about invoking a Lambda function from S3, see Tutorial: Using an Amazon S3 trigger to invoke a Lambda function.&quot;, &quot;Lambda functions can run on a schedule and read from S3 buckets. However, a scheduled/polling process would not process the S3 objects as soon as they arrive.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;Lambda functions can be invoked from S3 events and can read from S3 buckets. An event-based invocation would allow for the S3 objects to be processed as soon as they arrive. For more information about invoking a Lambda function from S3, see Tutorial: Using an Amazon S3 trigger to invoke a Lambda function.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;Lambda functions can be invoked from S3 events and can read from S3 buckets. An event-based invocation would allow for the S3 objects to be processed as soon as they arrive. For more information about invoking a Lambda function from S3, see Tutorial: Using an Amazon S3 trigger to invoke a Lambda function.&quot;, &quot;explanations&quot;: {&quot;A&quot;: &quot;Lambda functions can connect to Amazon EFS file systems. However, Amazon EFS file system changes cannot invoke Lambda functions. For more information about using Lambda functions with Amazon EFS, see Using Amazon EFS with Lambda.&quot;, &quot;B&quot;: &quot;Lambda functions can run on a schedule and connect to Amazon EFS file systems. However, a scheduled/polling process would not process the files as soon as they arrive. For more information about using Lambda functions with Amazon EFS, see Using Amazon EFS with Lambda.&quot;, &quot;C&quot;: &quot;Lambda functions can be invoked from S3 events and can read from S3 buckets. An event-based invocation would allow for the S3 objects to be processed as soon as they arrive. For more information about invoking a Lambda function from S3, see Tutorial: Using an Amazon S3 trigger to invoke a Lambda function.&quot;, &quot;D&quot;: &quot;Lambda functions can run on a schedule and read from S3 buckets. However, a scheduled/polling process would not process the S3 objects as soon as they arrive.&quot;}}\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 5 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 1 of 5</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">click an option</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">A company has an inventory system that receives sporadic inventory updates from a fulfillment system in the form of large JSON files. While many files can be sent in a short time period, days can pass when no files are sent. The company wants to process these files as soon as they arrive. Which solution will meet these requirements?</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Lambda functions can connect to Amazon EFS file systems. However, Amazon EFS file system changes cannot invoke Lambda functions. For more information about using Lambda functions with Amazon EFS, see Using Amazon EFS with Lambda.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Lambda functions can run on a schedule and connect to Amazon EFS file systems. However, a scheduled/polling process would not process the files as soon as they arrive. For more information about using Lambda functions with Amazon EFS, see Using Amazon EFS with Lambda.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Lambda functions can be invoked from S3 events and can read from S3 buckets. An event-based invocation would allow for the S3 objects to be processed as soon as they arrive. For more information about invoking a Lambda function from S3, see Tutorial: Using an Amazon S3 trigger to invoke a Lambda function.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Lambda functions can run on a schedule and read from S3 buckets. However, a scheduled/polling process would not process the S3 objects as soon as they arrive.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Exam Strategy Session 5 Answer Key</div></div>",
