    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-magenta);\" data-correct=\"B\" data-multi=\"\" data-rationale=\"The Lambda environment can reuse the same database connection for subsequent invocations when defining the database connection details in the code but outside the handler method. For more information about reusing the Lambda execution environment, see AWS Lambda execution environment.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;A developer needs to query a relational database from an AWS Lambda function. The Lambda function will be called frequently. The developer needs to avoid the latency introduced by the initial JDBC connection to the database in subsequent invocations of the Lambda function. How can the developer ensure the database connection is reused by Lambda?&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;Database connection details can be stored as an environment variable. However, the developer still needs to initialize the connection within the code for the connection to be used in queries. For more information about Lambda function environment variables, see Using AWS Lambda environment variables.&quot;, &quot;The Lambda environment can reuse the same database connection for subsequent invocations when defining the database connection details in the code but outside the handler method. For more information about reusing the Lambda execution environment, see AWS Lambda execution environment.&quot;, &quot;Database connection details can be stored in Systems Manager Parameter Store. However, initializing the connection within the handler method will result in it re-initializing each subsequent Lambda function invocation. For more information about storing parameters in AWS, see AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store.&quot;, &quot;Initializing the connection within the handler method will result in it re-initializing each subsequent Lambda function invocation.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;The Lambda environment can reuse the same database connection for subsequent invocations when defining the database connection details in the code but outside the handler method. For more information about reusing the Lambda execution environment, see AWS Lambda execution environment.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;The Lambda environment can reuse the same database connection for subsequent invocations when defining the database connection details in the code but outside the handler method. For more information about reusing the Lambda execution environment, see AWS Lambda execution environment.&quot;, &quot;explanations&quot;: {&quot;A&quot;: &quot;Database connection details can be stored as an environment variable. However, the developer still needs to initialize the connection within the code for the connection to be used in queries. For more information about Lambda function environment variables, see Using AWS Lambda environment variables.&quot;, &quot;B&quot;: &quot;The Lambda environment can reuse the same database connection for subsequent invocations when defining the database connection details in the code but outside the handler method. For more information about reusing the Lambda execution environment, see AWS Lambda execution environment.&quot;, &quot;C&quot;: &quot;Database connection details can be stored in Systems Manager Parameter Store. However, initializing the connection within the handler method will result in it re-initializing each subsequent Lambda function invocation. For more information about storing parameters in AWS, see AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store.&quot;, &quot;D&quot;: &quot;Initializing the connection within the handler method will result in it re-initializing each subsequent Lambda function invocation.&quot;}}\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 5 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 2 of 5</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">click an option</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">A developer needs to query a relational database from an AWS Lambda function. The Lambda function will be called frequently. The developer needs to avoid the latency introduced by the initial JDBC connection to the database in subsequent invocations of the Lambda function. How can the developer ensure the database connection is reused by Lambda?</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Database connection details can be stored as an environment variable. However, the developer still needs to initialize the connection within the code for the connection to be used in queries. For more information about Lambda function environment variables, see Using AWS Lambda environment variables.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">The Lambda environment can reuse the same database connection for subsequent invocations when defining the database connection details in the code but outside the handler method. For more information about reusing the Lambda execution environment, see AWS Lambda execution environment.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Database connection details can be stored in Systems Manager Parameter Store. However, initializing the connection within the handler method will result in it re-initializing each subsequent Lambda function invocation. For more information about storing parameters in AWS, see AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Initializing the connection within the handler method will result in it re-initializing each subsequent Lambda function invocation.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div>